 BSE|
 BSE| Printed optical absorption spectrum to local files, e.g. 
 BSE| BSE-TDA-eta=2.000.spectrum              
 BSE| as well as photoabsorption cross section to, e.g. 
 BSE| BSE-TDA-eta=2.000.crosssection          
 BSE| using the Eq. (7.51) from C. Ullrichs Book on TDDFT:
 BSE|
 BSE|    Im{α_{avg}(ω)} = -Im{\sum_{n=1}^{N_exc} \frac{f_n}{(ω+iη)² - (Ω^n)²}
 BSE|
 BSE| or for the full polarizability tensor:
 BSE|    α_{µ µ'}(ω) =  -\sum_n [2 Ω^n d_µ^n d_µ'^n] / [(ω+iη)²- (Ω^n)²]
 BSE|
 BSE| as well as Eq. (7.48):
 BSE|    σ_{µ µ'}(ω) = 4πω Im{α_{µ µ'}(ω)} / c
 BSE|
 BSE| with transition moments d_µ^n, oscillator strengths f_n,
 BSE| excitation energies Ω^n and the speed of light c.
 BSE|
 BSE| Please note that we adopt an additional minus sign for both quantities,
 BSE| due to the convention for charge vs particle density as done in MolGW:
 BSE| https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cpc.2016.06.019.
 BSE|
 BSE| Exciton descriptors for excitation level n are given by
 BSE|
 BSE|         d_eh   = | <r_h - r_e>_exc |
 BSE|
 BSE|         σ_e    = sqrt( <r_e^2>_exc - <r_e>_exc^2 )
 BSE|
 BSE|         σ_h    = sqrt( <r_h^2>_exc - <r_h>_exc^2 )
 BSE|
 BSE|         COV_eh = <r_e r_h>_exc - <r_e>_exc <r_h>_exc
 BSE|
 BSE|         d_exc  = sqrt( | < |r_h - r_e|^2 >_exc )
 BSE|                = sqrt( d_eh^2 + σ_e^2 + σ_h^2 - 2 * COV_eh )
 BSE|
 BSE|         R_eh   = COV_eh / (σ_e * σ_h)
 BSE|
 BSE| where the expectation values <.>_exc are taken with respect to the 
 BSE| exciton wavefunction  of excitation n:
 BSE|
 BSE|              𝚿_n(r_e,r_h) = Σ_{i,a} X_ia^n ψ_i(r_h) ψ_a(r_e)  ,
 BSE|
 BSE| i.e.
 BSE|
 BSE|              < O >_exc = < 𝚿_n | O | 𝚿_n > / < 𝚿_n | 𝚿_n >  ,
 BSE|
 BSE| where c_n = < 𝚿_n | 𝚿_n > = 1 within TDA.
 BSE|
 BSE|
 BSE| Here, we introduced
 BSE|
 BSE| ψ_i:   occupied molecular orbitals,
 BSE| ψ_a:   empty molecular orbitals and
 BSE|   r:   position operator.
 BSE|
 BSE| Ref.: Eqs. (28)-(32)
 BSE| Phys. Rev. B 113, 205152 (2026); https://doi.org/10.1103/38k2-d55h
 BSE|
 BSE|
